#!|
  A private function and a private constant, both declared and never used.

  This is rejected. Reachability is required of every item — public and
  private alike, functions, constants, types, and native declarations — and
  an item nothing reachable from `main` needs has no reason to have been
  written.

  `pub` is not an exemption. Exempting it would make one word the way to
  silence this diagnostic, and Cinnabar grants no mechanism to bypass,
  suppress, weaken, or defer an invariant. That is why an earlier attempt at
  this check was reverted: it exempted `pub`, and the only remedy it left
  anyone was to mark demonstration code public until the compiler stopped
  objecting.

  Both diagnostics are asserted in `tests/rejection_diagnostics.rs`, so
  losing either one fails rather than passing on its sibling.
|#

fun unused_helper() I64
  return 1
end

const UNUSED_CONST: I64 = 5

pub fun main() I64
  return 0
end
